WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.702
Range is useful when the repetition is based on numbers rather than an existing list.

00:00:05.702 --> 00:00:11.332
Range five produces zero, one, two, three, and four.

00:00:11.332 --> 00:00:14.192
The stop value is not included.

00:00:14.192 --> 00:00:20.886
Range one to six produces one through five, and a third argument can control the step size.

00:00:21.337 --> 00:00:25.794
The important detail is that Python often starts counting at zero.

00:00:25.794 --> 00:00:32.632
That may feel unusual at first, but it appears throughout indexing, loops, and many libraries.
